cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CaptureForge: a general-purpose, organism-agnostic hybridization-capture
  probe (bait) design pipeline
message: If you use CaptureForge, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adu
    given-names: Bright
    affiliation: "Genomics and Bioinformatics Core Facility, Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research, University of Ghana, Legon, Ghana"
abstract: >-
  CaptureForge is a reusable, end-to-end Nextflow (DSL2) pipeline that turns a
  gene list plus per-gene design intent into order-ready biotinylated-bait oligo
  sequences and a full QC/design report. It is disease- and organism-agnostic:
  any gene list and (where feasible) any reference genome are supported by
  changing inputs and config only, with no code edits.
keywords:
  - hybridization capture
  - bait design
  - probe design
  - targeted sequencing
  - nextflow
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-13
